==Trivia==
* Though [[Rabbit|Rabbit's]] speed boost helps with making Buddha's transformation more mobile, the speed boost is lower in percentage compared to when the user is untransformed. 
* Buddha's unawakened total damage reduction when stacked with full body [[Aura]] is 54%, while the awakened form is 61%.
** Using [[Water Body]] while wearing the [[Leviathan Shield]] and transforming into an awakened Buddha will stack the user's damage reduction up to 90%.
* Unawakened Buddha moves can be used while in awakened form. However, awakened moves cannot be used in unawakened form.
* Although this [[Blox Fruits|fruit]] is named Buddha, its icon is actually based off the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Budai Budai], the laughing monk often mistaken for the real Buddha.
* The Traditional Chinese characters around the aura of the awakened version of {{Ability|Z|1}} mean: 草 (grass), 体 (body), 心 (heart), 魂 (soul), 火 (fire), 水 (water), 風 (wind), and 岩 (stone).
** Similarly, the symbols in the outer circle are derived from Elder Futhark runes, and they represent ᛓ (wealth), ᚨ (god), ᚷ (gift), ᛖ (horse), ᛟ (heritage), ᛈ (pear-tree), ᛝ (the god Ingwaz), ᛗ (man), ᛢ (yew-tree), ᛉ (elk), ᛃ (good year), ᚹ (joy), ᛋ (sun), ᛞ (day), ᚱ (journey), and ᛒ (birch). The same symbols are used in the [[Colosseum Quest]].
* Buddha's {{Ability|X}} and {{Ability|V}} uses the same sound effect as one of the [[Sea Beast#Abilities|Sea Beast]]'s Water Beam moves.
* If the user is in Buddha's form while using [[Race Awakening]] as [[Rabbit#Version 4|Rabbit]] race, the user's hair will turn golden instead of white.
* If the user is in Buddha's form while using [[Race Awakening]] as [[Angel]], their sets of wings will turn golden.
* When using Buddha and turning [[Aura]] on, the user's head will not be affected by the [[Aura]]. If the user de-transforms with [[Aura]] active, their head may still not be affected.
* In the shop, Buddha is labeled as a fruit that "Can M1" despite the fruit not having an M1. However, many say that Buddha's M1 is the fighting style, sword or gun.

